; ============================================================================
; x.1sav.n64 - the save chip an N64 cartridge carries
;
; An extension key for the Universal Saves Format, defined by these
; specifications under a name reserved in the Vendor Names registry because
; which chip a game saves to is the cartridge's, not any emulator's.
;
; Unlike every other key, this one is checked as part of the bundle. The chip
; fixes how long the payload beside it is, and an `n64` bundle's `cartridge`
; save part has to carry it. The page says where.
;
; The root here is the value carried under the key, not a bundle. A bundle
; validates against the format's own schema whatever this holds, since an
; extension value is `any` there; this file is what makes the shape checkable.
; Like the format's schema, it describes one version exactly, so an integer
; key it does not list fails here and is round-tripped by a decoder.
; ============================================================================

n64 = {
  0 => chip, ; chip - the save memory the cartridge has
}

; Each name fixes the payload's length, in bytes.
chip = "eeprom-4k"  ;    512
     / "eeprom-16k" ;   2048
     / "sram-256k"  ;  32768
     / "sram-768k"  ;  98304, three banks of 32 KiB
     / "flash-1m"   ; 131072
     / "sram-1m"    ; 131072, homebrew only
